@startuml USER-FLOWS-customer
' Customer Support CRM — user flows. READ-ONLY DOCUMENTATION, nothing here is invented.
' Drawn from the repository at commit 969bb31 (2026-09-01): the Angular routes and guards,
' the ASP.NET Core controllers and their authorization policies, the Application services,
' the EF Core entities and migrations, and the approved documents under docs/ and .squad/.
' Red text marks what is NOT IMPLEMENTED. Index of all 11 diagrams: docs/USER-FLOWS.md
' Diagram 6 of 11 — Customer lifecycle in the Customer Portal
title Customer — Customer Portal self-service lifecycle

skinparam shadowing false
|#E8F0FE|Customer (browser)|
|#FFF4E5|API — api/v1|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|

|Customer (browser)|
start
if (has an account ?) then (no)
  :/auth/register — self-registration;
  |API — api/v1|
  :POST /auth/register  «anonymous»;
  |SQL Server|
  :INSERT Users(role = Customer) + Customers\non the configured default branch (A-15);
  |API — api/v1|
  :201 AuthToken — signed in immediately;
else (yes)
  :/auth/login → POST /auth/login → 200 AuthToken;
endif

|Customer (browser)|
:roleRedirectGuard → /portal (PortalShell)\n→ /portal/requests/new;
note right
  A Customer is not "at least an Agent", so no staff
  screen is ever loaded — /workspace and /admin are
  separate lazy chunks behind their own guards (AD-14),
  and their endpoints answer 403 regardless.
  Portal navigation today: Submit a request · Help.
end note

repeat
  if (what next ?) then (submit a request — T2-B)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /config → categories (code and name only —\nthe category → department map is staff-only, AP-17)\nand the feedback rating scale;
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Exactly four inputs (ui-design §7.2): subject,\ndescription, category, and a "this is urgent" checkbox —\nan indication, never a priority (A-17).\nNo department, no priority, no SLA wording (UI-11);
    |API — api/v1|
    :POST /portal/tickets\nAuthenticated submission only (A-9);
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT Ticket — status New, department derived from\nthe category (A-14), priority server-derived, SLA due\ndates computed once and frozen (A-20);\nround-robin auto-assignment → Notification(TicketAssigned);
    |Customer (browser)|
    :201 → navigate to /portal/requests/{id};

  elseif (read or reply to a request ?) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /portal/tickets/{id}/messages\nAnother customer's ticket → 404 (AP-4).\nInternal notes are unreachable by path (AP-5);
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Thread plus reply composer. Channel and author role\nare omitted from the portal payload (UI-11).\nNothing polls — this is not chat (T3-B);
    |API — api/v1|
    :POST /portal/tickets/{id}/messages {body};
    |SQL Server|
    :INSERT TicketMessage(direction = Inbound, channel = Portal)\nINSERT TicketActivity(MessagePosted)\nINSERT Notification(CustomerReplied) → staff;
    if (what was the status ?) then (Pending)
      |SQL Server|
      :UPDATE Tickets.Status = Open in the SAME transaction\nINSERT TicketActivity(StatusChanged), attributed to\nthe replying customer (R-13, R-14);
      |Customer (browser)|
      :The response envelope {message, ticketStatus, statusChanged}\ndrives the "reopened" cue in place — no re-fetch, no guess;
    elseif (Closed or Cancelled) then
      :<color:#B71C1C>409 ticket-terminal (A-5)</color>;
    else (New / Open / Resolved)
      :Status unchanged. A reply never reopens a Resolved\nrequest — that is the explicit transition A-16 grants,\nand its control is story 13's;
    endif

  elseif (help centre — T2-E) then (yes)
    |API — api/v1|
    :GET /portal/kb/articles?q=...\nGET /portal/kb/articles/{id};
    |SQL Server|
    :SELECT KnowledgeArticles WHERE IsPublished = 1\nAND Visibility = Public (constraint 19).\nAn internal or unpublished id → 404;
    |Customer (browser)|
    :Self-service search and article reader\n(/portal/help and /portal/help/:id);

  else (nothing else exists yet)
    :<color:#B71C1C>NOT IMPLEMENTED for a Customer today (story 13, T2-F):</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· /portal/requests — the "My requests" list</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  (/portal lands on requests/new instead)</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· Cancel-own-request and reopen-resolved controls —</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  the A-16 authority exists server-side, no UI calls it</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· Portal attachments, and the satisfaction / feedback control</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>· A customer notification feed — excluded by design:</color>\n<color:#B71C1C>  A-13's four notification types are staff-facing</color>;
  endif
repeat while (continue ?) is (yes) not (no)

|Customer (browser)|
:Sign out — client-side only (AP-8);
stop
@enduml
